// parity-expected-stdout-begin
// 3
// 2
// parity-expected-stdout-end

// Polymorphic recursion meets specialisation (0.0.8 plan, step 2a-3a).
//
// `depth` is called at `Int` and at `String`, so it is cloned: `depth$Int`
// binds `x` unboxed. Its self-call is at `List<Int>`, not `Int`, so it must
// not call `depth$Int`, which would hand a boxed list to a parameter it reads
// as a raw integer. It calls the generic `depth`, which every boxed type
// shares.
//
// Its pair is annot_polymorphic_recursion.flx, which recurses the same way
// at one boxed type and so is never cloned.

fn depth<a>(x: a, n: Int) -> Int {
    if n == 0 { 0 } else { depth([x], n - 1) + 1 }
}

fn main() with IO {
    print(depth(1, 3))
    print(depth("s", 2))
}
